# Settings of the quickstart stack. Copy to deploy/quickstart/.env (git ignores it) and fill it in:
#   cp deploy/quickstart/example.env deploy/quickstart/.env && chmod 600 deploy/quickstart/.env
# Only documentation names and addresses below (example.com, RFC 5737) — replace every one.

# --- Your OpenID Connect provider (PocketID, Authentik, Keycloak, …) ---
# Register a client there with the redirect URL https://<TS_AUTH_HOST>/auth/oidc/callback.
TS_OIDC_ISSUER=https://id.example.com
TS_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=tinysesam
TS_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=CHANGE_ME
# Restrict who may pass (recommended): a group at the provider, then add `groups` to the scopes.
# TS_ALLOWED_GROUPS=staff
# TS_OIDC_SCOPES=openid profile email groups

# --- TLS mode: acme | dns | internal | ip (deploy/quickstart/Caddyfile explains each) ---
TS_TLS=acme

# Public domain (acme) or internal domain (dns, internal): two names, both pointing to this host.
TS_AUTH_HOST=auth.example.com
TS_APP_HOST=app.example.com
TS_APP_PORT=443
# Single sign-on across subdomains. Leave it empty for TS_TLS=ip (a cookie domain cannot name an IP address).
TS_COOKIE_DOMAIN=.example.com

# TS_TLS=dns only — needs a Caddy with the provider's module (deploy/forward-auth/caddy-gate/Dockerfile).
# TS_DNS_PROVIDER=cloudflare
# TS_DNS_API_TOKEN=CHANGE_ME

# TS_TLS=ip instead (home network without a domain, docs/HOME-NETWORK.md) — the LAN address of this host, twice:
# TS_AUTH_HOST=192.0.2.10
# TS_APP_HOST=192.0.2.10
# TS_APP_PORT=8443
# TS_COOKIE_DOMAIN=

# --- Optional ---
# Your own application instead of the example (service name:port in this stack).
# TS_APP_UPSTREAM=app:9000
# OAuth for MCP clients such as Claude Code (README "OAuth for MCP clients"):
# TS_OAUTH_RESOURCES=https://app.example.com/mcp
# Services without a person (README "A service calls a protected app"), needs TS_OAUTH_RESOURCES; a pairing code:
#   docker compose exec tinysesam python -m tinysesam.gateway pair <account> --create-service
# TS_OAUTH_SERVICE_CLIENTS=1
# Links in the top bar of the gateway's pages (JSON list of [title, target] pairs):
# TS_TOPBAR_LINKS='[["App", "https://app.example.com/"]]'
# WebDAV behind the gate (T-66, README "App passwords"): the WebDAV server of this stack as the application, and app
# passwords for its host — each user creates one on the account page (https://<TS_AUTH_HOST>/auth/account) and signs
# in with it from rclone, a file manager or a phone. Add `header_up -Authorization` to the application's reverse_proxy
# in the Caddyfile (see the `@basic` branch there).
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=webdav
# TS_APP_UPSTREAM=webdav:9000
# TS_FORWARD_APPS={"app.example.com": {"name": "Files", "app_passwords": true}}
